   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "The gerund (-ando/-iendo) attaches a second, simultaneous action to a main verb — governments built railroads while considering them a symbol of progress, or a pattern reveals itself when you look carefully at the map. It's the natural tool for describing one process unfolding alongside, or as a consequence of, another. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "title": "What you already know",
+      "content": "You know the gerund for parallel and simultaneous actions from B1 Unit 2 (*caminaba escuchando música*). The gerund says what someone does while doing something else, or how they do it. It fits trains that carried goods and immigrants who arrived looking for work."
