-          "spanish": "Una nación es una comunidad imaginada porque la inmensa mayoría de sus miembros nunca se conocerán entre sí.",
-          "english": "A nation is an imagined community because the vast majority of its members will never meet each other."
+          "spanish": "El país en el que gobernaban no tenía identidad común.",
+          "english": "The country in which they governed had no common identity."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Esa construcción, que consistía en crear símbolos, relatos y rituales compartidos, no era un proceso natural.",
-          "english": "That construction, which consisted of creating shared symbols, stories and rituals, was not a natural process."
+          "spanish": "Los grupos de los que formaban parte eran pequeños.",
+          "english": "The groups they were part of were small."
         }
       ]
     },
     {
       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "Consistir en always takes en before its complement (consiste EN un grupo, consistía EN crear) — a common error is dropping the en, but the verb needs it to introduce what something is made up of."
+      "content": "The article agrees with the noun you describe (*el país*, *la comunidad*, *los grupos*), and the preposition is the one the verb needs: *pertenecer a*, *vivir en*, *formar parte de*. Never leave it out: not *el país que pertenecían*."
     }
   ]
 }
