+  "title": "The passive with ser: how heroes were presented",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "A closing thesis often combines several structures from this unit in one sentence — a relative clause, a ni... ni... sino contrast, a chain of passive participles — to state a considered judgment rather than just list facts. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "title": "What you already know",
+      "content": "You know the passive with *ser* + past participle from B1 Unit 18 (*la ley fue aprobada*). The participle agrees with the subject. It fits books and monuments well: what was written, put up or presented, often without saying by whom."
+    },
+    {
+      "type": "table",
+      "title": "ser + participle",
+      "rows": [
+        [
+          "Los héroes fueron presentados como padres de la patria.",
+          "*fueron presentados*: plural masculine"
+        ],
+        [
+          "La novela fue publicada en 1867.",
+          "*fue publicada*: singular feminine"
+        ],
+        [
+          "Las estatuas fueron puestas en las plazas.",
+          "*fueron puestas*: plural feminine"
+        ]
+      ]
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
+      "title": "In context",
       "items": [
         {
-          "spanish": "Todas las naciones son comunidades imaginadas; ese hecho no las hace menos reales para quienes las viven y las defienden.",
-          "english": "All nations are imagined communities; that fact doesn't make them any less real for those who live in and defend them."
+          "spanish": "Los libros de historia fueron escritos por autores.",
+          "english": "The history books were written by authors."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "El nacionalismo debe estudiarse ni como una verdad eterna ni como una simple mentira, sino como un proceso histórico concreto.",
-          "english": "Nationalism should be studied neither as an eternal truth nor as a simple lie, but as a concrete historical process."
+          "spanish": "Los héroes fueron presentados como padres de la patria.",
+          "english": "The heroes were presented as fathers of the nation."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Recorrimos varias piezas de ese proceso: una bandera improvisada, un himno elegido por concurso, y fronteras que dividieron a comunidades enteras.",
-          "english": "We covered several pieces of that process: an improvised flag, an anthem chosen by competition, and borders that divided entire communities."
+          "spanish": "La novela María fue publicada en 1867.",
+          "english": "The novel María was published in 1867."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Comprendido así, el nacionalismo deja de ser un simple telón de fondo y se convierte en uno de los proyectos más ambiciosos del periodo.",
-          "english": "Understood this way, nationalism stops being a mere backdrop and becomes one of the era's most ambitious projects."
+          "spanish": "Sus nombres fueron dados a calles y escuelas.",
+          "english": "Their names were given to streets and schools."
         }
       ]
     },
     {
       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "Ni... ni... sino... is the structure for rejecting two extremes at once before proposing a third position — useful whenever an argument's real point is \"it's neither of the easy answers, but this more complicated one instead.\""
+      "content": "The participle agrees with the subject in gender and number: *el libro fue escrito*, *la novela fue publicada*, *los héroes fueron presentados*. The doer, if named, comes after *por*: *fueron escritos por autores*."
     }
   ]
 }
